WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.322
Use this self-check without looking back at the code first.

00:00:03.322 --> 00:00:07.967
Explain the main concepts in your own words and give one small example.

00:00:07.967 --> 00:00:11.822
If you can explain why a pattern works and when you would use it,

00:00:11.822 --> 00:00:16.257
that is stronger evidence of understanding than remembering the exact syntax.

00:00:16.257 --> 00:00:19.412
Connect the concept to a small analytics task.

00:00:19.412 --> 00:00:24.487
Imagine the value came from a sales file, survey, or operational system.

00:00:24.487 --> 00:00:32.097
Ask whether Python is interpreting it correctly and whether another person could understand the calculation

00:00:32.097 --> 00:00:33.632
from the names and output.

00:00:33.632 --> 00:00:37.862
Before moving on, explain the main idea in one sentence without reading the slide.

00:00:37.862 --> 00:00:43.282
That quick explanation is a useful check that the concept is becoming reusable knowledge.
